# Two Telegram destinations, one bot.
#
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_DM is where the pipeline asks you to decide something: the two
# approval gates, plus arbitration and stuck escalations. Keep it quiet — the
# whole value of that channel is that every message in it needs you.
#
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_JOURNAL is the running story of each idea: what was proposed
# and why, the approved rule animation before table play, what the checkers
# said verbatim, and what a repair actually changed.
# It is chatty by design, nothing in the pipeline ever reads it back, and it
# is nowhere on disk — the story exists only in that chat.
#
# Either can be left unset: messages print to the terminal instead, which is
# how you read them before setting up a bot at all.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_DM=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_JOURNAL=

# Optional: OrcaSlicer for the real slice check in gate.py. Without these the
# gate still runs every mesh check and simply skips slicing.
# ORCASLICER_CLI=/Applications/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer
# ORCA_PROFILE=/abs/machine.json;/abs/process.json;/abs/filament.json
